course: dictionary
lesson: 4660
title: Kitchen words in context
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: A hob is a word you may meet in a recipe, a kitchen safety sign or a cookery book. The sentences around it give you clues. «Hobs and pans stay hot long after they are switched off» tells you a hob is something that gets hot, and that it is used with pans.
explain: Read the whole sentence, then ask: what would fit here? «A boy in Auckland helping with pasta turns the pan handle inwards, so nobody can knock the boiling pot off the hob.» The hob is the place where the pot sits, so it must be the part of the cooker that heats the pan.
explain: Try your meaning in the sentence instead of the hard word. Does «the pot sits on the flat top of the cooker» still make sense? Yes, so you have probably found the right meaning. If you are still unsure, a dictionary will settle it.
fact: A hob is the flat top part of a cooker where you put pans to heat food.
fact: In the USA and Canada, a hob is often called a stovetop or cooktop.
fact: «Hobs and pans stay hot long after they are switched off.» Always treat them as hot until they have cooled.
fact: «Gas hobs burn gas in rings of small flames, and electric hobs heat with elements.»
fact: An induction hob uses a magnetic field to heat the pan itself, so the glass stays cooler than the pan.
exercise: What is a hob? | A cupboard where plates are kept | A small oven for bread | A tap that runs hot water | *The flat top part of a cooker where you heat pans
exercise: «Hobs and pans stay hot long after they are switched off, so pan handles are turned inward.» Why do we turn pan handles inward? | *So nobody can knock the pan off the hob | So the handle gets cooler | So the pan can heat faster | So the pan looks tidy in a photo
exercise: «An induction hob uses a magnetic field to heat the pan itself.» Which part gets hot on an induction hob? | *The pan | The glass top only | The kitchen air | The tea towel
test: In the USA and Canada, a hob is often called what? | A sink | A dishwasher | A fridge | *A stovetop
test: «A dark glass hob can burn you minutes after it is switched off.» What is the danger? | *It can still be hot after it is switched off | It always glows bright red | It is cold if it looks dark | It only burns in winter
exam: «Never leave a pan alone on a hot hob, and children should cook on the hob only with an adult.» What should a child do? | Cook alone while the hob is hot | Put tea towels on the hob to dry | Lean over the hob to reach the pan | *Cook on the hob only with an adult
